       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">FINANCE</span> · BS Personal Finance · 2026-10-29 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>Adani Ports Shares Surge 4% Following Strong Q2 Results</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#finance</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Adani Ports and Special Economic Zone (APSEZ) shares rose 4% to ₹1,823.15 after reporting a 17% year-on-year increase in profit to ₹3,682 crore for Q2FY27. Consolidated revenue grew 24% to ₹11,340 crore, driven by strong performances in international ports and marine business segments.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-29/adani-ports-shares-surge-4-following-strong-q2-results.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Following a robust first half, the company raised its FY27 revenue guidance to ₹44,000–₹46,000 crore and EBITDA guidance to ₹26,000–₹27,000 crore. Additionally, FY27 capital expenditure guidance was increased by ₹3,000 crore to support long-term infrastructure goals, including expanding port capacity to one billion metric tonnes.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief effectively captures the financial results, guidance revisions, and strategic outlook mentioned in the source.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
