       <h1>Airbnb Hosts Inaugural Nonprofit Gala in Los Angeles</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#tech</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Airbnb held its inaugural nonprofit gala in Los Angeles on October 28, featuring celebrity guests including Serena Williams and Demi Lovato. The event, hosted by Jimmy Kimmel, marked a new initiative where the company will donate 10 cents from every booking to its nonprofit, aiming to raise $500 million over five years to fund free housing for families in need.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-29/airbnb-hosts-inaugural-nonprofit-gala-in-los-angeles.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>While the gala drew confusion from social media users regarding the company's decision to host such an event, Airbnb stated the evening was intended to honor supporters. The nonprofit provides temporary housing for families impacted by disasters, domestic violence, and medical needs.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief accurately summarizes the gala's purpose, the donation initiative, and the context of the public reaction provided in the source.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://techcrunch.com/2026/10/29/where-was-my-invite-to-the-wait-what-airbnb-had-a-gala/" rel="noopener">TechCrunch</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
