       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">SPORTS</span> · BBC Sport · 2026-10-29 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>Australia nears Test win after South Africa's poor batting</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#sports</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Australia moved closer to a series victory in the third Test in Cape Town as South Africa’s top order struggled on day three. South Africa reached 140-4 at the close, holding a narrow 40-run lead after gifting wickets through careless shots.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-29/australia-nears-test-win-after-south-africas-poor-batting.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Openers Aiden Markram and David Bedingham fell to poor decision-making, with Bedingham dismissing for the second time in the match by pulling into the hands of a fielder. Captain Temba Bavuma also fell to a wild swipe, leaving the Proteas in a precarious position against the Australian bowling attack.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief effectively summarizes the cricketing action and the specific dismissals mentioned in the source.</p>
