       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · News18 India · 2026-10-29 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>BJP's Kedarnath Singh Concedes Varanasi Graduate MLC Poll Defeat</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>BJP candidate Kedarnath Singh has conceded defeat in the Varanasi Graduates’ constituency election for the Uttar Pradesh Legislative Council. Samajwadi Party candidate Ashutosh Sinha currently leads the race by approximately 17,000 votes, with counting of second-preference ballots ongoing since October 27.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-29/bjps-kedarnath-singh-concedes-varanasi-graduate-mlc-poll-def.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>In a Facebook post, Singh accepted the public mandate with humility, framing the loss as an integral part of the democratic process. Meanwhile, SP president Akhilesh Yadav has instructed his party workers to remain at the counting center until they receive official victory certificates.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief effectively summarizes the election outcome and the reactions of both the candidate and the SP leader.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.news18.com/india/accept-public-mandate-bjps-kedarnath-singh-concedes-defeat-in-varanasi-graduate-mlc-polls-ws-l-10402636.html" rel="noopener">News18 India</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       <div class="cityguide"><b>City guide</b><p>More on <a href="https://bharatdn.com/city/varanasi/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Varanasi</a> - census 2011 population, live weather and air quality, local food and getaways.</p></div>
