     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-10-29 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Ennore Residents Criticize Government Performance on Pollution</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Ennore residents have issued a negative report card for the state government for the second consecutive year, citing failures in wetland restoration and pollution control. The assessment of 24 government bodies found that five agencies, including the Energy Department and the CMDA, failed to meet any of their committed obligations.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-29/ennore-residents-criticize-government-performance-on-polluti.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Residents highlighted ongoing issues such as fly-ash leaks, illegal industrial emissions, and a mass fish kill in Ennore Creek that saw no official report. The report also identified gaps in local healthcare and infrastructure, noting that promised fisheries markets remain incomplete and local residents continue to face exposure to harmful chemical pollutants.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief clearly identifies the government bodies involved and the specific environmental grievances cited by residents.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/cities/chennai/ennore-residents-report-card-for-govt-flags-gaps-in-wetlandrestoration-pollution-control/article71640851.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
