     <article class="story single" data-beat="business">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">BUSINESS</span> · BBC Business · 2026-10-29 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Farmer Criticizes Budget Minimum Wage Hike as 'Massive Blow'</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#business</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Chancellor John Healey announced a 3.9% minimum wage increase in the recent Budget, intended to provide cost-of-living relief. However, Tristan Bennett of Bennetts Farms described the measure as a 'massive blow' to his hospitality and cafe operations, noting the difficulty of making such businesses profitable under current pressures.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-29/farmer-criticizes-budget-minimum-wage-hike-as-massive-blow.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>While Bennett welcomed the increase in the small business rate relief threshold to £18,000, he expressed disappointment over the lack of VAT reductions for the hospitality sector. Other small business owners, such as bookshop co-owner Rachel Buchanan, also characterized the Budget as 'tinkering around the edges' rather than providing substantial relief.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Accurately attributes the criticism and correctly identifies the specific figures mentioned in the source.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c6zxj9qy4yg8o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" rel="noopener">BBC Business</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
       <div class="sharebar" data-href="/article/2026-10-29/farmer-criticizes-budget-minimum-wage-hike-as-massive-blow" data-title="Farmer Criticizes Budget Minimum Wage Hike as 'Massive Blow'"><b>Share:</b>
