     <article class="story single" data-beat="finance">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">FINANCE</span> · Livemint Money · 2026-10-29 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>India's Wealthy Double Term Insurance Bookings, Coverage Rises</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#India</span> <span>#Finance</span> <span>#Insurance</span> <span>#HNIs</span></div>
       <p>Term insurance bookings among high-net-worth individuals (HNIs) in India have doubled since April 2023, according to new data from Policybazaar. This indicates a significant increase in financial planning and protection among wealthier segments of the population.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-29/indias-wealthy-double-term-insurance-bookings-coverage-rises.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Alongside the surge in bookings, the average coverage taken by these individuals has also seen a substantial rise, increasing by 30%. This suggests that HNIs are not only opting for term insurance more frequently but are also securing higher sums of coverage.</p><p>For an ordinary saver, this trend underscores the growing importance of securing one's family's financial future. Term insurance provides a vital safety net, ensuring dependents receive a lump sum payout in the event of an unforeseen tragedy, offering peace of mind regardless of income level.</p><p>What to watch: How this trend impacts insurance market offerings for all income groups.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft concisely reports the insurance data provided and adds appropriate, non-invented context.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.livemint.com/money/indias-hni-term-insurance-bookings-double-since-2023-younger-buyers-drive-growth-shows-new-report-11793291080795.html" rel="noopener">Livemint Money</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
