       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · News18 India · 2026-10-29 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Manoj Tiwari Claims Partial Yamuna Cleanup; AAP Challenges Results</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>BJP MP Manoj Tiwari claimed that nearly 30 kilometers of the Yamuna river in Delhi has been cleaned ahead of the Chhath festival. During a site visit, Tiwari cited the presence of birds as evidence of improved water quality and announced plans for upcoming dredging to assist navigation.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-29/manoj-tiwari-claims-partial-yamuna-cleanup-aap-challenges-re.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The Aam Aadmi Party (AAP) has disputed these claims, with leader Saurabh Bharadwaj challenging Tiwari to drink water from the Kalindi Kunj Ghat. Tiwari stated his efforts are intended to improve the river for Delhi residents rather than serve as a political attack against former Chief Minister Arvind Kejriwal.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Covers the core conflict and the specific claims made by both Tiwari and Bharadwaj clearly and concisely.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.news18.com/india/cleaned-almost-30-km-of-river-manoj-tiwari-takes-yamuna-dip-aap-says-drink-water-at-kalindi-kunj-10403711.html" rel="noopener">News18 India</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
