       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">TECH</span> · TechCrunch · 2026-10-29 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Meta Launches AI Fashion App Style Sketch</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#tech</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Meta has quietly released Style Sketch, an AI-powered fashion app currently available in Indonesia, Singapore, and Thailand. The app integrates with Instagram to build a virtual wardrobe from existing photos or manual uploads, allowing users to generate outfit combinations and view virtual try-ons on a model matched to their body type.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-29/meta-launches-ai-fashion-app-style-sketch.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Beyond wardrobe management, the tool provides weather-based outfit planning and travel itinerary suggestions. This release follows CEO Mark Zuckerberg’s strategy to accelerate app development through AI-driven efficiencies. Meta has not yet confirmed plans for a wider international rollout of the application.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief is accurate and captures the core functionality and release details. It misses mentioning the app also works on Facebook, but remains highly dense.</p>
