     <article class="story single" data-beat="world">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">WORLD</span> · The Hindu World · 2026-10-29 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Pentagon Fires Top Military Planner Amid Trump’s Iran Strike Talk</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Pentagon</span> <span>#Pete Hegseth</span> <span>#Brett Sylvia</span> <span>#Iran</span></div>
       <p>U.S. Defence Secretary Pete Hegseth dismissed Lt Gen Brett Sylvia, the head of strategy, plans and policy (J5) on the Joint Chiefs of Staff, on October 28, 2026, according to a defence official who spoke on condition. Sylvia becomes the second J5 director removed under Hegseth, following Lt Gen Joseph McGee’s forced retirement in October 2025.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-29/pentagon-fires-top-military-planner-amid-trumps-iran-strike-.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The anonymous official said no immediate replacement has been named and no reason was offered for Sylvia’s removal. A Joint Staff spokesperson expressed “deepest gratitude” for Sylvia’s 32 years of service and wished his family well, while noting his duties typically involve generating and coordinating military plans for the Chairman, the Joint Chiefs and the President.</p><p>The firing comes as President Donald Trump repeatedly floated new strikes against Iran, vowing to “finish the job” after the eight‑month war that began with Israel. Trump has hinted at fresh attacks after the U.S. midterm elections on November 3, while U.S. missions in West Asia issued alerts warning of possible Iran‑backed retaliation. A third aircraft carrier and thousands of troops are moving toward the region, and diplomats say allies should brace for extended conflict.</p><p>Sylvia’s biography, now removed from official sites, listed his command of the 101st Airborne Division at Fort Campbell until May 2025 and a prior stint as vice director for J5. Hegseth has earlier ordered a 20 % cut in senior officer ranks by Jan 1, 2027, reducing roughly 800 flag and general officer slots, a move critics label a “purge”. Sen Mark Kelly warned the cuts could take a generation to recover. What to watch: whether Trump authorises new Iran strikes following the midterms.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft accurately synthesizes the firing of Lt Gen Sylvia and the broader context of military leadership changes and regional tensions.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/hegseth-fires-pentagons-top-military-planner-even-as-trump-considers-new-iran-strikes/article71639041.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu World</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
       <div class="sharebar" data-href="/article/2026-10-29/pentagon-fires-top-military-planner-amid-trumps-iran-strike-" data-title="Pentagon Fires Top Military Planner Amid Trump’s Iran Strike Talk"><b>Share:</b>
