       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">FINANCE</span> · BS Personal Finance · 2026-10-29 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Sensex and Nifty rise over 1% on strong Q2 earnings and easing crude</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Markets</span> <span>#Economy</span> <span>#Investment</span> <span>#FMCG</span></div>
       <p>Indian stock markets recorded a gain of over 1 percent, driven by strong quarterly results and falling crude oil prices. The rally was further supported by optimism surrounding potential US-Iran peace talks and increased buying by foreign investors.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-29/sensex-and-nifty-rise-over-1-on-strong-q2-earnings-and-easin.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Sectoral performance was led by realty and fast-moving consumer goods (FMCG) stocks, which outperformed the broader market. Positive corporate earnings provided a fundamental underpinning for the index gains, while the decline in crude prices helped reduce inflationary pressures and input costs for businesses.</p><p>For ordinary investors, the rise in indices reflects broader market sentiment improving due to both domestic corporate performance and favorable external geopolitical developments. The participation of foreign investors suggests renewed confidence in the Indian market’s outlook amid these tailwinds.</p><p>What to watch: Follow-through on foreign investment flows and the impact of continued crude price stability on corporate margins.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft accurately reflects all information provided in the source summary without adding unnecessary fluff.</p>
