     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-10-29 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>Tamil Nadu to Launch Pilot Model Registration Hubs</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>The Tamil Nadu government has sanctioned five Model Registration Hubs (MRH) in Chennai, Chengalpattu, and Coimbatore districts at a cost of ₹7.84 crore. These pilot facilities will allow citizens to register property documents and marriages regardless of the specific Sub-Registrar Office jurisdiction.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-29/tamil-nadu-to-launch-pilot-model-registration-hubs.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Managed by a third-party service provider, the hubs will offer standard and premium registration services with fees ranging from ₹2,000 to ₹10,000. While the state plans to expand this jurisdiction-free initiative to 20 additional locations, all statutory registration processes will remain under the authority of the respective Sub-Registrars.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief is accurate, concise, and captures all critical financial and operational details from the source.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
