     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · News18 India · 2026-10-29 · editor 9/10 · 2 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Tripura Electoral Roll Revision Deferred Second Time Ahead of Civic Polls</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Tripura</span> <span>#Elections</span> <span>#Electoral Roll</span> <span>#ECI</span></div>
       <p>The Election Commission of India (ECI) has deferred the Special Intensive Revision (SIR) of electoral rolls in Tripura for the second time, pushing the publication of the final voter list to April 7, 2027. This decision, announced by the Chief Electoral Officer (CEO), Tripura, on Thursday, October 29, 2026, follows the ECI's approval of the state's request to postpone the exercise, citing upcoming urban local body elections. The qualifying date for the revision remains January 1, 2027.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-29/tripura-electoral-roll-revision-deferred-second-time-ahead-o.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>This latest revision alters the timeline for all major stages of the SIR process. Preparatory work, including training of election personnel and printing of materials, is now scheduled from December 15 to December 24, 2026. House-to-house visits by Booth Level Officers (BLOs) will occur from December 26, 2026, to January 25, 2027. The draft electoral roll is set for publication on February 1, 2027, with the period for filing claims and objections running until March 2, 2027. The notice phase and disposal of claims and objections will conclude by April 1, 2027, leading to the final electoral roll's publication on April 7, 2027.</p><p>The deferment accommodates Tripura's preparations for elections to 21 urban local bodies, including the Agartala Municipal Corporation. According to Tripura Times, the State Election Commission is organizing for these civic polls, with the election schedule anticipated to be announced shortly. The ECI's approval of this deferment explicitly acknowledged the upcoming general elections to urban local bodies in the state.</p><p>This marks the second postponement of the SIR exercise. The initial revision process, first scheduled to begin on September 5, 2026, with a final electoral roll publication by December 23, was first deferred to accommodate village committee elections under the Tripura Tribal Areas Autonomous District Council (TTAADC), held on September 28. That postponement shifted preparatory work to October 27-November 5, house-to-house visits to November 6-December 5, and final publication to February 15, 2027. The most recent deferment further extends the exercise into 2027, allowing the election machinery to focus on the civic polls before the intensive voter-list revision, as reported by TripuraInfo.</p><p>What to watch: The announcement of the election schedule for Tripura's urban local bodies.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft is accurate and comprehensive, covering all logistical details and the context of the deferment.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.news18.com/india/tripura-sir-rescheduled-fresh-timeline-out-house-to-house-visits-from-december-26-ws-lr-10404141.html" rel="noopener">News18 India</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
