     <article class="story single" data-beat="cricket">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">CRICKET</span> · ESPN Cricinfo · 2026-10-29 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>Warrican Five-Wicket Haul Stalls Bangladesh</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#cricket</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Jomel Warrican claimed five wickets on the second morning of the Test match, triggering a collapse in the Bangladesh batting lineup. Despite a resilient 105 from Shadman, Bangladesh lost five wickets for just 19 runs to be bowled out for 272.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-29/warrican-five-wicket-haul-stalls-bangladesh.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Litton Das remained unbeaten on 34 as the innings concluded. The hosts entered the second day looking to build on their position, but the West Indies bowling attack successfully halted their momentum. The match continues as both teams navigate the remaining sessions of the Test.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief accurately summarizes the key statistics and the nature of the batting collapse reported in the source.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.cricinfo.com/ci/content/story/1560518.html?ex_cid=OTC-RSS" rel="noopener">ESPN Cricinfo</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
