     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-10-29 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>Yadgir Postal Division Hosts Integrity Awareness Rally</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>The Yadgir Postal Division conducted an awareness rally themed ‘Integrity for Prosperity’ on October 28 to promote ethical standards and a corruption-free administration. Starting at the divisional postal office near Ambedkar Circle, the procession concluded at Babu Jagjivan Ram Circle, with participants advocating for transparency in public life.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-29/yadgir-postal-division-hosts-integrity-awareness-rally.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Assistant Superintendent Krishna Mohite flagged off the event, emphasizing that honesty and accountability are essential for societal prosperity. Speakers urged government employees to maintain high ethical principles in daily administration and ensure the responsible utilization of state resources.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief is concise, accurate, and captures the key details and themes of the event described in the source.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
