       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-10-29 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>YSRCP Mayoral Candidate Seeks Re-election in Vijayawada</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>YSRCP mayoral candidate Rayana Bhagyalakshmi has appealed to Vijayawada voters for another term, citing significant development during the party's previous five-year tenure. She highlighted improvements to drainage, water tanks, and the Ajit Singh Nagar dumping yard as key achievements.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-29/ysrcp-mayoral-candidate-seeks-re-election-in-vijayawada.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>During her campaign, Bhagyalakshmi and party leaders criticized the current coalition government for failing to address civic issues like flooding. The YSRCP is urging voters to support all 86 of its corporator candidates in the upcoming municipal elections to continue the party's development agenda.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief accurately summarizes the political context and the candidate's campaign claims as reported in the source.</p>
